>> title: Carrot Cake
>> category: Cakes & Loaves
>> tags: carrot, cream cheese, spice, oven
>> servings: 12
>> time: 2 hr 30 min

Grease a #9x13-in pan{}.

Preheat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C).

Whisk @eggs{4%large}, @granulated sugar{1%cup}(200 g), @light brown sugar{1%cup}(200 g), @vegetable oil{1%cup}(240 mL), @vanilla extract{2%tsp}(10 mL).

Whisk @all-purpose flour{2%cup}(250 g), @baking soda{2%tsp}(12 g), @ground cinnamon{2%tsp}(6 g), @table salt{1%tsp}(6 g).

Fold @&(~1)dry mixture{}, @grated carrots{3%cup}(330 g; about 5 medium) into @&(3)egg mixture{}.

Bake @&(~1)batter{} at 350°F for ~{40%min}, then cool completely.

Beat @cream cheese{8%oz}(225 g; softened), @unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g; softened), @powdered sugar{3%cup}(340 g) until smooth.

Spread @&(~1)frosting{} over @&(6)cooled cake{}.
